  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 171154\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n200 AM HST Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nWestern East Pacific:\nA tropical wave continues to produce disorganized showers and\nthunderstorms well to the south-southwest of the southern tip of the\nBaja California Peninsula. Environmental conditions appear\nconducive for gradual development of this system, and a tropical\ndepression is likely to form this weekend or early next week as it\nmoves westward at 10 to 15 mph across the western part of the East\nPacific.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...20 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...high...70 percent.\n\nWell East-Southeast of the Hawaiian Islands (Former TD15-E):\nShowers and thunderstorms have increased somewhat with an area of\nlow pressure related to the remnants of Tropical Depression\nFifteen-E. Environmental conditions appear only marginally conducive\nfor some development of this system as it moves gradually westward,\nremaining east-southeast of the Hawaiian Islands.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...10 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...10 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Papin\nNNNN",
